<%# The turn is not over until the stream says so, and neither a long answer
    nor a slow tool says anything about itself while it is happening. This row
    is the page's "still working" — the state the TUI pins to its own edge.

    It is drawn for a live turn and hidden by class once the stream closes, so
    the last frame of a finished turn keeps no clock that goes on counting. -%>
<p class="row working" data-since="<%= h(since) %>" data-threshold="0">
  <span class="mark working" aria-hidden="true">◐</span>
  <span class="label">Working…</span>
  <span class="live-clock"></span>
</p>
